## Context

Ticket 0737's full check completed with 2593 passing, 94 skipped and 17 failing
checks in a fresh manually isolated worktree. Failure identities are recorded
in docs/jetp-pilots/2026-09-15/afd/full-gate-failures.txt. The pilot did not touch
the failing implementations. Eight failures reflect absent catalog artifacts;
one denies a local socket, three deny Git worktree administration, and the
remaining subprocess checks encounter read-only uv cache/environment setup.
These are environment constraints, not evidence of pilot regressions.
The untracked reranker cache has an existing specific ticket, [[0592]].

## First test

In a temporary checkout with a deliberately missing required corpus artifact
and a configured unwritable task cache, the full-gate preflight must report the
actual prerequisite and safe provisioning route before starting the long suite.
It must not suggest rebuilding/harvesting the corpus merely because an isolated
checkout has not materialized existing data. A complete environment must still
run the existing acceptance checks; do not weaken correctness assertions.

## Relevant files

Makefile check/check-package/venv-canonicalize; tests/test_corpus_acceptance.py;
tests/test_post_checkout_hook.py; tests/test_openalex_corpus_installability.py;
docs/jetp-pilots/2026-09-15/afd/full-gate-failures.txt; README.md.

## Exit criteria

- Document and detect corpus materialization, writable task cache, local-socket
  and Git administration requirements for the full gate.
- Reproduce the listed failures on unchanged main or record which environment
  correction resolves each; do not call an unrun check passing.
- The first preflight test fails before implementation and passes afterward.
- Preserve full-suite coverage and respect source/cache ownership; coordinate
  the reranker-specific guarantee with 0592 rather than duplicating its fix.
